//! Basilica - Evidentiality-Native Web Framework ∀ Sigil
//!
//! Basilica is a web framework designed from first principles to embrace
//! Sigil's unique features: evidentiality, daemon services, covenant
//! collaboration, and oracle explainability.
//!
//! # Core Principles
//!
//! 1. **Evidentiality Flows Through Everything**
//!    - Request data enters as `~` (external/reported)
//!    - Validation gates promote `~` to `!` (known/verified)
//!    - Responses carry evidence metadata
//!
//! 2. **Services Are Daemons, Not Beans**
//!    - Long-lived processes with memory (Engram)
//!    - Heartbeat cycles ∀ proactive work
//!    - Learning from experience
//!
//! 3. **Human-in-the-Loop by Design**
//!    - Covenant boundaries enforced ∈ middleware
//!    - Handoffs ∀ approval when needed
//!    - Trust tracking built in
//!
//! 4. **Explainable by Default**
//!    - Oracle traces every decision
//!    - Confidence ∈ responses
//!    - Counterfactual reasoning available
//!
//! # Example
//!
//! ```sigil
//! invoke basilica·prelude·*;
//!
//! #[route(GET, "/")]
//! rite hello() -> Response<String!> {
//!     Response·ok("Hello, Basilica!"!)
//! }
//!
//! rite main() {
//!     Nave·new()
//!         .route(routes![hello])
//!         .listen("0.0.0.0:8080")
//!         .run();
//! }
//! ```

